# Workspace Recipe Docs

Inspect, validate, preview, and render recipes.

## When To Use It

- Before creating shaped files.
- After editing recipes or templates.
- When checking mapped module roles.

## How To Respond

- List and show recipes first.
- Use `enclosure workspace recipe <name> <path> --shell` as the convention oracle.
- Use dry runs before writing.
- Compose reusable `fragment` recipes with `includes`.
- Keep module-to-role ownership in `workspace.recipe.roles_map`.
- Use `--drifts` to compare mapped trees to recipes.
- Write bench HTML to a caller-provided path such as `reports/<name>.html` or `/tmp/<name>.html`.
- Never pass flags such as `--help`, `--docs`, or `--llm` as `--html`.

## Related Commands

- `enclosure workspace recipe --help`
- `enclosure workspace recipe --list`
- `enclosure workspace recipe --check`
- `enclosure workspace recipe --bench <module> --html reports/module-bench.html`
- `enclosure workspace recipe --bench-all --html reports/workspace-bench.html`
- `enclosure workspace rules --docs`
